 * T2 money page — the #1 build priority (J-05: "Recurring for sure then
 * termites and commercial"). Hand-written to exemplar depth.
 *
 * Sources: C-01, C-11 (products), E-02 (pricing), E-04 (no contracts),
 * E-09/E-10 (guarantee), K-01 (customer questions verbatim), K-02, K-03,
 * K-05–K-07, F-14 (voice). Biology cited to Texas A&M AgriLife.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AnswerBox from '../../components/AnswerBox.astro';
import Trust from '../../components/Trust.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import SpokeLinks from '../../components/SpokeLinks.astro';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../../data/services';
import { TOWNS } from '../../data/towns';

const svc = serviceBySlug('pest-control')!;
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Services', path: '/services/' },
  { name: 'Recurring Pest Control', path: '/services/pest-control/' },
];

const quickAnswer =
  'Recurring pest control from Trusted Termite and Pest Solutions runs bi-monthly or quarterly across Gaines County and the Permian Basin. Service is generally $140 to $160 per visit with a $200 to $250 initial. No contracts, and re-services between visits are free for covered pests.';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How much do you charge for pest control?',
    a: 'Recurring residential service is generally around $140 to $160 or more per visit, depending on the size of the home, the pest pressure and how often you want service. The initial visit is usually $200 to $250 because it is more extensive — inspecting the property, treating the interior where it is needed and doing a thorough exterior. Pricing depends on square footage and what is actually going on, so we would rather understand the problem first and give you an accurate number than hand everyone the same quote.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the treatment safe for my kids and pets?',
    a: 'Yes. We use professional pest-control products and apply them according to their EPA-approved labels. We take into account children, pets and the areas your family regularly uses when deciding how and where products are applied, and we will tell you about any precautions that need to be taken before or after treatment rather than leaving you to work it out.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to leave the house while you spray?',
    a: 'For most general pest-control services, no. We do ask that people and pets stay off treated areas until the product has completely dried. Certain specialised treatments have different requirements, and if that is the case we explain the instructions before we begin.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does it take to start working?',
    a: 'It depends on the pest and the product. Some pests start dying very quickly. Other treatments are designed on purpose to work over time so the pest carries the material back to where it is nesting — that is how you get a colony rather than the few you can see. It is also normal with some treatments to see activity briefly increase as pests are disturbed and come out of hiding.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How often should I have the house treated?',
    a: 'Bi-monthly or quarterly for ongoing protection. Which one depends on the property, the pressure, the time of year and what is around you — a house backing onto a field in Gaines County is a different proposition from one in the middle of a Midland subdivision. Regular service means staying ahead of problems rather than waiting until you have an infestation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'If I still see bugs after you spray, will you come back?',
    a: 'Yes. We stand behind the work with a 30-day service guarantee, and recurring customers also get service between their scheduled visits when they need it. If you are having an issue between services, call and we will get it taken care of. We would much rather come back out than have you sit with it until the next appointment.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does general pest control actually cover?',
    a: 'A general service typically covers common crawling insects — ants, spiders, cockroaches and other household pests. Certain pests need a separate treatment plan: termites, bed bugs, fleas, ticks, rodents and other specialised problems each have their own approach and their own terms.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you treat inside and outside, or just outside?',
    a: 'On the initial service we typically treat both, so we establish a good starting point. After that, recurring service focuses mainly on maintaining the exterior barrier and addressing conditions around the home. Interior treatment is still available whenever it is needed or whenever you ask for it.',
  },
